{"assets":["/statement-assets/b5749d0daf69ad978ea2d77b7045e5ea744205ff95c413145dca4d94cacd3826.png"],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1055","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"F. Tree and XOR"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"4 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You are given a connected undirected graph without cycles (that is, a tree) of $$$n$$$ vertices, moreover, there is a non-negative integer written on every edge."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Consider all pairs of vertices $$$(v, u)$$$ (that is, there are exactly $$$n^2$$$ such pairs) and for each pair calculate the bitwise exclusive or ("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"xor"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":") of all integers on edges of the simple path between $$$v$$$ and $$$u$$$. If the path consists of one vertex only, then xor of all integers on edges of this path is equal to $$$0$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Suppose we sorted the resulting $$$n^2$$$ values in non-decreasing order. You need to find the $$$k$$$-th of them."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The definition of "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"xor"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" is as follows."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Given two integers $$$x$$$ and $$$y$$$, consider their binary representations (possibly with leading zeros): $$$x_k \\dots x_2 x_1 x_0$$$ and $$$y_k \\dots y_2 y_1 y_0$$$ (where $$$k$$$ is any number so that all bits of $$$x$$$ and $$$y$$$ can be represented). Here, $$$x_i$$$ is the $$$i$$$-th bit of the number $$$x$$$ and $$$y_i$$$ is the $$$i$$$-th bit of the number $$$y$$$. Let $$$r = x \\oplus y$$$ be the result of the "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"xor"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" operation of $$$x$$$ and $$$y$$$. Then $$$r$$$ is defined as $$$r_k \\dots r_2 r_1 r_0$$$ where:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"$$$$$$ r_i = \\left\\{ \\begin{aligned} 1, ~ \\text{if} ~ x_i \\ne y_i \\\\ 0, ~ \\text{if} ~ x_i = y_i \\end{aligned} \\right. $$$$$$"}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains two integers $$$n$$$ and $$$k$$$ ($$$2 \\le n \\le 10^6$$$, $$$1 \\le k \\le n^2$$$) — the number of vertices in the tree and the number of path in the list with non-decreasing order."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Each of the following $$$n - 1$$$ lines contains two integers $$$p_i$$$ and $$$w_i$$$ ($$$1 \\le p_i \\le i$$$, $$$0 \\le w_i \\lt 2^{62}$$$) — the ancestor of vertex $$$i + 1$$$ and the weight of the corresponding edge."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Print one integer: $$$k$$$-th smallest xor of a path in the tree."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"2 1\n1 3\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"0\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"3 6\n1 2\n1 3\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"2\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The tree in the second sample test looks like this:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/b5749d0daf69ad978ea2d77b7045e5ea744205ff95c413145dca4d94cacd3826.png"},"kind":"image"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For such a tree in total $$$9$$$ paths exist: "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":true},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$1 \\to 1$$$ of value $$$0$$$ "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$2 \\to 2$$$ of value $$$0$$$ "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$3 \\to 3$$$ of value $$$0$$$ "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$2 \\to 3$$$ (goes through $$$1$$$) of value $$$1 = 2 \\oplus 3$$$ "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$3 \\to 2$$$ (goes through $$$1$$$) of value $$$1 = 2 \\oplus 3$$$ "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$1 \\to 2$$$ of value $$$2$$$ "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$2 \\to 1$$$ of value $$$2$$$ "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$1 \\to 3$$$ of value $$$3$$$ "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$3 \\to 1$$$ of value $$$3$$$ "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"F","problemCode":"1055F","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1055/problem/F"}